\mt1 THE EPISTLE OF PAUL THE APOSTLE TO THE ROMANS  
\c 14  
\p
\v 1 Him that is \w weak\w* in the \w faith\w* receive \w ye\w*, \add but\add* \w not\w* \w to\w* \w doubtful\w* \w disputations\w*.  
\v 2 \w For\w* \w one\w* \w believeth\w* that he may \w eat\w* all \w things\w*: \w another\w*, who is \w weak\w*, \w eateth\w* \w herbs\w*.  
\v 3 \w Let\w* \w not\w* him that \w eateth\w* \w despise\w* him that \w eateth\w* \w not\w*; \w and\w* \w let\w* \w not\w* him which \w eateth\w* \w not\w* \w judge\w* him that \w eateth\w*: \w for\w* \w God\w* hath \w received\w* \w him\w*.  
\v 4 \w Who\w* \w art\w* \w thou\w* that \w judgest\w* another \w man’s\w* \w servant\w*? to his \w own\w* \w master\w* he \w standeth\w* \w or\w* \w falleth\w*. \w Yea\w*, he shall be holden \w up\w*: \w for\w* \w God\w* \w is\w* \w able\w* to \w make\w* \w him\w* \w stand\w*.  
\v 5 One \w man\w* \w esteemeth\w* one \w day\w* \w above\w* \w another\w*: \w another\w* \w esteemeth\w* \w every\w* \w day\w* \add alike\add*. \w Let\w* every \w man\w* be fully \w persuaded\w* \w in\w* his \w own\w* \w mind\w*.  
\v 6 He that \w regardeth\w* the \w day\w*, \w regardeth\w* \add it\add* unto the \w Lord\w*; \w and\w* he that \w regardeth\w* \w not\w* the \w day\w*, to the \w Lord\w* he \w doth\w* \w not\w* \w regard\w* \add it\add*. He that \w eateth\w*, \w eateth\w* to the \w Lord\w*, \w for\w* he \w giveth\w* \w God\w* \w thanks\w*; \w and\w* he that \w eateth\w* \w not\w*, to the \w Lord\w* he \w eateth\w* \w not\w*, \w and\w* \w giveth\w* \w God\w* \w thanks\w*.  
\v 7 \w For\w* \w none\w* of \w us\w* \w liveth\w* to \w himself\w*, \w and\w* no \w man\w* \w dieth\w* to \w himself\w*.  
\v 8 \w For\w* \w whether\w* we \w live\w*, we \w live\w* unto the \w Lord\w*; \w and\w* \w whether\w* we \w die\w*, we \w die\w* unto the \w Lord\w*: \w whether\w* we \w live\w* \w therefore\w*, \w or\w* \w die\w*, we \w are\w* the \w Lord’s\w*.  
\v 9 \w For\w* \w to\w* this \w end\w* \w Christ\w* \w both\w* \w died\w*, \w and\w* \w rose\w*, \w and\w* \w revived\w*, \w that\w* he might be \w Lord\w* \w both\w* of the \w dead\w* \w and\w* \w living\w*.  
\v 10 \w But\w* \w why\w* \w dost\w* \w thou\w* \w judge\w* \w thy\w* \w brother\w*? \w or\w* \w why\w* \w dost\w* \w thou\w* set at \w nought\w* \w thy\w* \w brother\w*? \w for\w* we \w shall\w* \w all\w* \w stand\w* before the judgment \w seat\w* of \w Christ\w*.  
\v 11 \w For\w* it is \w written\w*, \add As\add* \w I\w* \w live\w*, \w saith\w* the \w Lord\w*, \w every\w* \w knee\w* shall \w bow\w* to \w me\w*, \w and\w* \w every\w* \w tongue\w* shall \w confess\w* to \w God\w*.  
\v 12 \w So\w* \w then\w* every \w one\w* of \w us\w* shall \w give\w* \w account\w* \w of\w* \w himself\w* to \w God\w*.  
\v 13 Let \w us\w* \w not\w* \w therefore\w* \w judge\w* one \w another\w* any \w more\w*: \w but\w* \w judge\w* \w this\w* \w rather\w*, \w that\w* no \w man\w* \w put\w* a \w stumblingblock\w* \w or\w* an occasion to \w fall\w* \w in\w* \add his\add* \w brother’s way\w*.  
\v 14 I \w know\w*, \w and\w* am \w persuaded\w* \w by\w* the \w Lord\w* \w Jesus\w*, \w that\w* \add there is\add* \w nothing\w* \w unclean\w* \w of\w* \w itself\w*: \w but\w* to him that \w esteemeth\w* any \w thing\w* to \w be\w* \w unclean\w*, to \w him\w* \add it is\add* \w unclean\w*.  
\v 15 \w But\w* \w if\w* \w thy\w* \w brother\w* be \w grieved\w* \w with\w* \add thy\add* \w meat\w*, \w now\w* walkest \w thou\w* \w not\w* \w charitably\w*. \w Destroy\w* \w not\w* \w him\w* \w with\w* \w thy\w* \w meat\w*, \w for\w* \w whom\w* \w Christ\w* \w died\w*.  
\v 16 \w Let\w* \w not\w* \w then\w* \w your\w* \w good\w* be evil spoken \w of\w*:  
\v 17 \w For\w* the \w kingdom\w* of \w God\w* \w is\w* \w not\w* \w meat\w* \w and\w* \w drink\w*; \w but\w* \w righteousness\w*, \w and\w* \w peace\w*, \w and\w* \w joy\w* \w in\w* \w the\w* \w Holy\w* \w Ghost\w*.  
\v 18 \w For\w* he \w that\w* \w in\w* these \w things\w* \w serveth\w* \w Christ\w* \add is\add* \w acceptable\w* to \w God\w*, \w and\w* \w approved\w* of \w men\w*.  
\v 19 Let \w us\w* \w therefore\w* follow \w after\w* the \w things\w* which make for \w peace\w*, \w and\w* \w things\w* wherewith one may \w edify\w* \w another\w*.  
\v 20 \w For\w* \w meat\w* \w destroy\w* \w not\w* the \w work\w* of \w God\w*. All \w things\w* \w indeed\w* \add are\add* \w pure\w*; \w but\w* \add it is\add* \w evil\w* for that \w man\w* who \w eateth\w* \w with\w* \w offence\w*.  
\v 21 \add It is\add* \w good\w* \w neither\w* to \w eat\w* \w flesh\w*, \w nor\w* to \w drink\w* \w wine\w*, \w nor\w* \add any thing\add* \w whereby\w* \w thy\w* \w brother\w* \w stumbleth\w*, \w or\w* is \w offended\w*, \w or\w* is made \w weak\w*.  
\v 22 \w Hast\w* \w thou\w* \w faith\w*? \w have\w* \add it\add* \w to\w* \w thyself\w* \w before\w* \w God\w*. \w Happy\w* \add is\add* he that \w condemneth\w* \w not\w* \w himself\w* \w in\w* that thing \w which\w* he \w alloweth\w*.  
\v 23 \w And\w* he that \w doubteth\w* is \w damned\w* \w if\w* he \w eat\w*, \w because\w* \add he eateth\add* \w not\w* \w of\w* \w faith\w*: \w for\w* \w whatsoever\w* \add is\add* \w not\w* \w of\w* \w faith\w* \w is\w* \w sin\w*.   
\c 16  
\p
\v 1 I \w commend\w* unto \w you\w* \w Phebe\w* \w our\w* \w sister\w*, which \w is\w* a \w servant\w* of the \w church\w* which \w is\w* \w at\w* \w Cenchrea\w*:  
\v 2 \w That\w* ye \w receive\w* \w her\w* \w in\w* the \w Lord\w*, as \w becometh\w* \w saints\w*, \w and\w* \w that\w* ye \w assist\w* \w her\w* \w in\w* \w whatsoever\w* \w business\w* she hath \w need\w* of \w you\w*: \w for\w* \w she\w* hath \w been\w* a \w succourer\w* of \w many\w*, \w and\w* of \w myself\w* \w also\w*.  
\v 3 \w Greet\w* \w Priscilla\w* \w and\w* \w Aquila\w* \w my\w* \w helpers\w* \w in\w* \w Christ\w* \w Jesus\w*:  
\v 4 \w Who\w* \w have\w* \w for\w* \w my\w* \w life\w* laid \w down\w* their \w own\w* \w necks\w*: unto \w whom\w* \w not\w* \w only\w* \w I\w* give \w thanks\w*, \w but\w* \w also\w* \w all\w* the \w churches\w* of the \w Gentiles\w*.  
\v 5 \w Likewise\w* \add greet\add* the \w church\w* that is \w in\w* \w their\w* \w house\w*. \w Salute\w* \w my\w* \w wellbeloved\w* \w Epaenetus\w*, \w who\w* \w is\w* the \w firstfruits\w* of \w Achaia\w* \w unto\w* \w Christ\w*.  
\v 6 \w Greet\w* \w Mary\w*, \w who\w* \w bestowed\w* \w much\w* \w labour\w* \w on\w* \w us\w*.  
\v 7 \w Salute\w* \w Andronicus\w* \w and\w* \w Junia\w*, \w my\w* \w kinsmen\w*, \w and\w* \w my\w* \w fellowprisoners\w*, \w who\w* \w are\w* of \w note\w* \w among\w* the \w apostles\w*, \w who\w* \w also\w* \w were\w* \w in\w* \w Christ\w* \w before\w* \w me\w*.  
\v 8 \w Greet\w* \w Amplias\w* \w my\w* \w beloved\w* \w in\w* the \w Lord\w*.  
\v 9 \w Salute\w* \w Urbane\w*, \w our\w* \w helper\w* \w in\w* \w Christ\w*, \w and\w* \w Stachys\w* \w my\w* \w beloved\w*.  
\v 10 \w Salute\w* \w Apelles\w* \w approved\w* \w in\w* \w Christ\w*. \w Salute\w* them which \w are\w* \w of\w* \w Aristobulus’\w* \add household\add*.  
\v 11 \w Salute\w* \w Herodion\w* \w my\w* \w kinsman\w*. \w Greet\w* them that \w be\w* \w of\w* \w the\w* \add household\add* of \w Narcissus\w*, which \w are\w* \w in\w* the \w Lord\w*.  
\v 12 \w Salute\w* \w Tryphena\w* \w and\w* \w Tryphosa\w*, who \w labour\w* \w in\w* the \w Lord\w*. \w Salute\w* the \w beloved\w* \w Persis\w*, \w which\w* \w laboured\w* \w much\w* \w in\w* the \w Lord\w*.  
\v 13 \w Salute\w* \w Rufus\w* \w chosen\w* \w in\w* the \w Lord\w*, \w and\w* \w his\w* \w mother\w* \w and\w* \w mine\w*.  
\v 14 \w Salute\w* \w Asyncritus\w*, \w Phlegon\w*, \w Hermas\w*, \w Patrobas\w*, \w Hermes\w*, \w and\w* the \w brethren\w* which are \w with\w* \w them\w*.  
\v 15 \w Salute\w* \w Philologus\w*, \w and\w* \w Julia\w*, \w Nereus\w*, \w and\w* \w his\w* \w sister\w*, \w and\w* \w Olympas\w*, \w and\w* \w all\w* the \w saints\w* which are \w with\w* \w them\w*.  
\v 16 \w Salute\w* one \w another\w* \w with\w* \w an\w* \w holy\w* \w kiss\w*. The \w churches\w* of \w Christ\w* \w salute\w* \w you\w*.   
\p
\v 17 \w Now\w* I \w beseech\w* \w you\w*, \w brethren\w*, \w mark\w* them which \w cause\w* \w divisions\w* \w and\w* \w offences\w* contrary \w to\w* the \w doctrine\w* \w which\w* \w ye\w* have \w learned\w*; \w and\w* \w avoid\w* \w them\w*.  
\v 18 \w For\w* they that are \w such\w* \w serve\w* \w not\w* \w our\w* \w Lord\w* \w Jesus\w* \w Christ\w*, \w but\w* their \w own\w* \w belly\w*; \w and\w* \w by\w* good \w words\w* \w and\w* fair \w speeches\w* \w deceive\w* the \w hearts\w* of the \w simple\w*.  
\v 19 \w For\w* \w your\w* \w obedience\w* is come \w abroad\w* \w unto\w* \w all\w* \add men\add*. I am \w glad\w* \w therefore\w* \w on\w* \w your\w* \w behalf\w*: but \w yet\w* I would \w have\w* \w you\w* \w wise\w* \w unto\w* that which is \w good\w*, \w and\w* \w simple\w* \w concerning\w* \w evil\w*.  
\v 20 \w And\w* the \w God\w* of \w peace\w* shall \w bruise\w* \w Satan\w* \w under\w* \w your\w* \w feet\w* \w shortly\w*. The \w grace\w* \w of\w* \w our\w* \w Lord\w* \w Jesus\w* \w Christ\w* \add be\add* \w with\w* \w you\w*. \w Amen\w*.   
\p
\v 21 \w Timotheus\w* \w my\w* \w workfellow\w*, \w and\w* \w Lucius\w*, \w and\w* \w Jason\w*, \w and\w* \w Sosipater\w*, \w my\w* \w kinsmen\w*, \w salute\w* \w you\w*.  
\v 22 \w I\w* \w Tertius\w*, who \w wrote\w* \add this\add* \w epistle\w*, \w salute\w* \w you\w* \w in\w* the \w Lord\w*.  
\v 23 \w Gaius\w* \w mine\w* \w host\w*, \w and\w* of \w the\w* \w whole\w* \w church\w*, \w saluteth\w* \w you\w*. \w Erastus\w* the \w chamberlain\w* of the \w city\w* \w saluteth\w* \w you\w*, \w and\w* \w Quartus\w* a \w brother\w*.  
\v 24 The \w grace\w* \w of\w* \w our\w* \w Lord\w* \w Jesus\w* \w Christ\w* \add be\add* \w with\w* \w you\w* \w all\w*. \w Amen\w*.   
\p
\v 25 \w Now\w* to him that is of \w power\w* to \w stablish\w* \w you\w* according \w to\w* \w my\w* \w gospel\w*, \w and\w* the \w preaching\w* of \w Jesus\w* \w Christ\w*, according \w to\w* the \w revelation\w* of the \w mystery\w*, which was kept \w secret\w* since the world \w began\w*,  
\v 26 \w But\w* \w now\w* is made \w manifest\w*, \w and\w* \w by\w* the \w scriptures\w* of the \w prophets\w*, according \w to\w* the \w commandment\w* of \w the\w* \w everlasting\w* \w God\w*, made \w known\w* \w to\w* \w all\w* \w nations\w* \w for\w* the \w obedience\w* of \w faith\w*:  
\v 27 To \w God\w* \w only\w* \w wise\w*, \add be\add* \w glory\w* \w through\w* \w Jesus\w* \w Christ\w* \w for\w* \w ever\w*. \w Amen\w*.   
\s1 Written to the Romans from Corinthus, \add and sent\add* by Phebe servant of the church at Cenchrea.
